WEBVTT

00:00:00.527 --> 00:00:03.685
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.685 --> 00:00:06.063
Being together like this...

00:00:06.063 --> 00:00:09.941
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.941 --> 00:00:13.362
Forever...

00:00:13.362 --> 00:00:15.864
...under this sky...

00:00:15.864 --> 00:00:18.158
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.161
In this beauty...

00:00:21.161 --> 00:00:22.287
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.287 --> 00:00:23.330
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.456
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.748 --> 00:00:26.083
With more dreaming...

00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:27.167
...and more loving...

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:28.251
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.251 --> 00:00:29.461
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:30.712
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.962 --> 00:00:33.131
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.131 --> 00:00:35.801
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.011
A lovely life every day...

00:00:38.011 --> 00:00:40.722
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.722 --> 00:00:42.766
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.766 --> 00:00:45.477
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.477 --> 00:00:47.604
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.604 --> 00:00:50.690
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.151 --> 00:00:56.530
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.865
If you go there...

00:00:58.865 --> 00:01:02.869
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.869 --> 00:01:06.248
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.248 --> 00:01:08.708
Under this sky...

00:01:08.708 --> 00:01:11.086
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.672 --> 00:01:16.133
Being together like this...

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:19.636
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.348 --> 00:01:25.851
Under this sky...

00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:28.103
...we'll walk together!

00:01:33.113 --> 00:01:36.450
Damn, this is tough...

00:01:38.953 --> 00:01:40.996
Oh no, I'm out of time!

00:01:41.538 --> 00:01:43.374
What am I supposed to do?!

00:01:43.832 --> 00:01:44.792
Cut it out already.

00:01:45.459 --> 00:01:47.962
How can you be so indecisive
over a boxed lunch?

00:01:48.295 --> 00:01:51.799
Because they all look really good...

00:01:51.924 --> 00:01:53.008
Make up your mind already!

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.928
Then, I'll have this, this, and this please.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:58.806
Hurry up!

00:01:59.181 --> 00:02:02.518
I know, but... Oh no, the doors are closing!

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.404
Jeez, you're such a loony.

00:02:13.904 --> 00:02:18.325
We're on our way to practice the
martial art of deep sea fishing.

00:02:18.993 --> 00:02:19.952
Get your act together, man!

00:02:22.997 --> 00:02:24.331
Excuse me,

00:02:25.624 --> 00:02:27.209
is this seat taken?

00:02:32.548 --> 00:02:34.216
No, no! Please, have a seat!

00:02:34.758 --> 00:02:35.384
Thanks.

00:02:41.306 --> 00:02:43.017
Are you brothers whom are traveling together?

00:02:43.475 --> 00:02:44.226
Brothers?

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.603
No, no, I mean we don't even look alike.

00:02:47.229 --> 00:02:49.356
Yeah, Kinta has these slanty eyes.

00:02:49.648 --> 00:02:50.399
Shut up!

00:02:51.984 --> 00:02:53.444
You guys are funny.

00:02:56.488 --> 00:02:57.531
How far are you going?

00:02:58.365 --> 00:02:59.950
To the last stop, Kamikeiha.

00:03:00.492 --> 00:03:02.369
Really? We're going there too!

00:03:02.828 --> 00:03:03.704
We're going deep sea fishing.

00:03:04.455 --> 00:03:05.330
Sounds like fun.

00:03:15.841 --> 00:03:20.429
Wow, I'd never have guessed you're the famous
picture book author, Kaori Minazuki!

00:03:21.388 --> 00:03:23.640
I loved your books when I was little!

00:03:23.766 --> 00:03:24.558
Thanks.

00:03:24.558 --> 00:03:27.603
I can't believe I'm friends with a real celebrity.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.813
You've only just started talking to her.

00:03:30.439 --> 00:03:31.648
A friend's a friend.

00:03:31.648 --> 00:03:33.776
<i>It's been nearly an hour... it's almost time.</i>

00:03:40.115 --> 00:03:42.201
Oh, my phone. Please, excuse me.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.789
Yes? I'm on the train right now, please wait
a moment while I head to the deck.

00:03:48.874 --> 00:03:53.670
Sorry, it's a business call, and it looks like it's
going to take a while. Could you watch my bag?

00:03:54.129 --> 00:03:55.130
Sure, no problem.

00:03:55.631 --> 00:03:56.173
Thanks.

00:04:00.135 --> 00:04:02.888
Nishiumigaoka, Nishiumigaoka.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.598
<i>It's finally time...</i>

00:04:05.974 --> 00:04:07.267
<i>I can't turn back now.</i>

00:04:20.697 --> 00:04:22.032
<i>I’ve got one hour,</i>

00:04:22.616 --> 00:04:25.702
<i>I've rehearsed this many times; it’ll work out.</i>

00:04:30.541 --> 00:04:33.293
What's her big idea, having me
come out to a place like this...

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:36.880
I just hope she's not trying to get me back.

00:04:38.132 --> 00:04:41.468
And sending me this pathetic threat...

00:04:41.969 --> 00:04:43.095
What's she thinking?

00:04:46.014 --> 00:04:50.435
Oh well, I'll just reveal her
identity and end her career.

00:04:58.402 --> 00:04:59.069
Kenji...

00:04:59.653 --> 00:05:02.072
Ah, how are you Ms. Minazuki?

00:05:02.322 --> 00:05:03.407
You're late.

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:06.410
Ms. Minazuki?

00:05:08.203 --> 00:05:11.248
What's with the formal tone?

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.628
I'm just not interested in another
relationship with you at this point.

00:05:51.788 --> 00:05:53.540
<i>I finally did it.</i>

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.875
<i>This will do.</i>

00:05:55.292 --> 00:05:55.876
<i>This...</i>

00:06:07.221 --> 00:06:09.014
<i>You’ve gotta hurry, Kaori.</i>

00:06:09.848 --> 00:06:11.350
<i>You still have over forty minutes left,</i>

00:06:11.975 --> 00:06:15.062
<i>Even if it takes longer than expected, you’ll be
at the station with fifteen minutes to spare.</i>

00:06:15.562 --> 00:06:18.982
<i>Then you just have to get on that train.</i>

00:06:18.982 --> 00:06:21.026
<i>It'll be alright; they'll never know!</i>

00:06:24.446 --> 00:06:28.450
<i>The people in the company know that Taga and
I have been fighting about our relationship.</i>

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.914
<i>If Taga’s found dead, I'll be a suspect as well.</i>

00:06:36.041 --> 00:06:41.672
<i>The police aren’t dumb enough to fall for the silly
letter I wrote disguising myself as a new author.</i>

00:06:43.215 --> 00:06:45.217
<i>That's why I’m using this alibi trick.</i>

00:06:52.266 --> 00:06:56.687
I'm sorry, but we're doing some construction
work here. Please use the old road over there.

00:06:57.396 --> 00:07:04.194
No way! If I can't use this road... I?"
have to go the long way round.

00:07:06.405 --> 00:07:07.614
I've got no time to waste.

00:07:17.791 --> 00:07:19.668
<i>If I miss that train, everything? over.</i>

00:07:20.836 --> 00:07:22.087
<i>I'm going to make it!</i>

00:07:27.759 --> 00:07:29.469
<i>There it is; I’ve gotta hurry!</i>

00:07:41.231 --> 00:07:45.861
This is a local train to Kamikeihan.

00:07:55.245 --> 00:07:56.872
Leaving for Kamikeihan.

00:07:57.831 --> 00:07:59.499
The doors are closing.

00:07:59.499 --> 00:08:03.337
Wait! Wait! Don't close them yet!

00:08:26.026 --> 00:08:26.902
I made it.

00:08:29.071 --> 00:08:30.864
<i>I did it!</i>

00:08:31.114 --> 00:08:32.199
<i>Everything? gone according to plan,</i>

00:08:33.116 --> 00:08:38.205
<i>Now, I’ll have been on this
train when he was killed.</i>

00:08:39.748 --> 00:08:44.795
<i>It’s okay. All I have to do now is ask
those two kids for their addresses.</i>

00:08:45.587 --> 00:08:48.298
<i>Even if I'm a suspect, I’ll have a rock-solid alibi,</i>

00:08:51.593 --> 00:08:52.010
WHAT?!

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.137
Ah! You surprised me!

00:08:55.097 --> 00:08:56.890
Did something happen? You look all serious.

00:08:57.557 --> 00:08:59.518
<i>Why is this kid here?</i>

00:09:00.477 --> 00:09:03.021
What are you doing out here anyway?

00:09:03.688 --> 00:09:07.442
I'm a bit nosy... What about you?

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:11.780
Oh, my call took longer than expected.

00:09:12.197 --> 00:09:13.824
Yeah, that was a long conversation.

00:09:14.825 --> 00:09:16.326
It's been a good hour.

00:09:16.868 --> 00:09:19.663
It must have been quite a heated conversation.

00:09:20.622 --> 00:09:22.040
Huh? What do you mean?

00:09:22.541 --> 00:09:26.545
Well, you're covered in sweat, even
though the air conditioner's on full.

00:09:27.796 --> 00:09:30.799
It's almost as if you ran in from outside.

00:09:35.429 --> 00:09:36.513
<i>He saw me.</i>

00:09:37.806 --> 00:09:40.058
<i>No. That can't <i>be.</i></i>

00:09:41.309 --> 00:09:42.894
Yeah, it was a really annoying conversation.

00:09:43.937 --> 00:09:46.148
My stupid editor told me to
redraw it and I got angry.

00:09:51.403 --> 00:09:52.946
That sure was a long conversation.

00:09:53.321 --> 00:09:57.492
Yeah, it just wouldn't end.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.204
Oh, who's that person next to you?

00:10:01.663 --> 00:10:03.039
Hey, don't be rude.

00:10:04.458 --> 00:10:07.377
Oh, he's my ex. I've been too busy to change it.

00:10:07.919 --> 00:10:10.839
But anyway, are you guys in high school?

00:10:14.176 --> 00:10:15.510
Ever heard of DDS?

00:10:16.428 --> 00:10:17.679
You mean Dan Morihiko’s...

00:10:19.264 --> 00:10:22.851
To be honest, we're DDS students.

00:10:23.351 --> 00:10:24.853
<i>What was that?!</i>

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.273
Kinta, we're not supposed to say that in public.

00:10:28.315 --> 00:10:30.358
Oh crap, it slipped.

00:10:32.986 --> 00:10:35.447
Don't worry, I won't tell anyone.

00:10:35.947 --> 00:10:37.657
Yes, no need to worry,

00:10:38.533 --> 00:10:42.287
<i>If these kids are DDS students,
they’re perfect for my alibi,</i>

00:10:43.205 --> 00:10:45.165
<i>I guess I’m lucky after all.</i>

00:10:47.334 --> 00:10:48.168
<i>What?!</i>

00:10:49.044 --> 00:10:50.670
<i>T- This...</i>

00:10:52.797 --> 00:10:53.507
<i>Back there, it...!</i>

00:10:54.174 --> 00:10:56.593
Do you want me to put that
up there by the bags?

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:00.889
No, no, don't bother. I actually
have to work on it now.

00:11:02.098 --> 00:11:03.808
What a nuisance!

00:11:05.435 --> 00:11:07.312
Wow, is this an original drawing?

00:11:07.437 --> 00:11:09.314
Hey, it's not done yet!

00:11:18.323 --> 00:11:21.493
Wow, that's amazing. It's so good.

00:11:21.493 --> 00:11:23.286
Yeah, that's great!

00:11:24.412 --> 00:11:25.080
Thanks.

00:11:26.831 --> 00:11:28.083
<i>This drawing...</i>

00:11:31.169 --> 00:11:32.671
Oh, it's my phone...

00:11:33.296 --> 00:11:34.172
Hello?

00:11:36.508 --> 00:11:37.259
Dan-Sensei?

00:11:37.634 --> 00:11:39.386
I'm going out to the deck.

00:11:40.845 --> 00:11:41.596
I'll come too.

00:11:48.728 --> 00:11:50.272
What? A case?

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.317
The victim was found near Nishiumigaoka.

00:11:55.318 --> 00:11:58.613
I want you guys to take part in the
investigation, as you're nearby.

00:11:59.406 --> 00:12:01.616
I'll send you the victim's details.

00:12:02.158 --> 00:12:02.784
Okay.

00:12:06.329 --> 00:12:06.788
There it is.

00:12:08.707 --> 00:12:09.874
It's a picture of the victim.

00:12:10.875 --> 00:12:11.501
This is...

00:12:12.669 --> 00:12:14.588
Ms. Minazuki's ex-boyfriend...

00:12:20.677 --> 00:12:25.724
Dan-Sensei, could it be that the victim
was stabbed with some sort of blade?

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.768
Hmm? Yes, that is, indeed, the case.

00:12:29.978 --> 00:12:30.645
So it's true...

00:12:31.521 --> 00:12:33.481
Kyuu-kun, how did you know that?

00:12:34.065 --> 00:12:40.196
Sir, the perpetrator might be with us right now.

00:12:41.823 --> 00:12:42.532
What?

00:12:43.408 --> 00:12:48.371
It could be the picture book author, Kaori
Minazuki, who's on the train with us.

00:12:49.789 --> 00:12:53.293
I understand. Please start your
investigation immediately.

00:12:54.002 --> 00:12:54.294
Yes!

00:12:56.338 --> 00:12:58.757
Hey, Kyuu, what are you talking about?

00:12:59.007 --> 00:13:01.217
She's been on this train the whole time.

00:13:01.801 --> 00:13:03.553
How could she have committed the murder?

00:13:04.929 --> 00:13:08.058
The whole time... Are you certain?

00:13:10.018 --> 00:13:15.065
Ms. Minazuki began to talk on the phone shortly
before we arrived at Nishiumigaoka,

00:13:15.982 --> 00:13:20.945
and I met her by chance on the deck,
shortly after we left Hamaokayama.

00:13:22.447 --> 00:13:26.034
She was on her knees, panting,
totally soaked with sweat.

00:13:27.577 --> 00:13:31.998
Furthermore, the train takes an hour to get from Nishiumigaoka, where the
victim was found, to Hamaokayama,

00:13:32.707 --> 00:13:35.460
but it only takes half an hour by car.

00:13:36.544 --> 00:13:37.379
Then...

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.633
She may have gotten off at
Nishiumigaoka, committed the crime,

00:13:41.633 --> 00:13:44.678
and driven her car to Hamaokayama,

00:13:44.678 --> 00:13:46.596
and gotten back on the train.

00:13:47.555 --> 00:13:52.727
Damn! She was planning on using us
as her alibi because we're from DDS.

00:13:53.812 --> 00:13:55.647
That name must have put
her on her toes, as well...

00:13:57.732 --> 00:14:01.986
I know! Let's test her by using "that"...

00:14:06.658 --> 00:14:09.244
<i>Fifteen minutes until we reach
the final stop, Kamikeihan.</i>

00:14:10.578 --> 00:14:12.414
<i>I found out about those kids, too.</i>

00:14:13.998 --> 00:14:18.002
<i>It sure looks like I’ve completely
covered my tracks.</i>

00:14:31.073 --> 00:14:32.450
It was a woman.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.659
No, a man.

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:35.453
You think so?

00:14:35.453 --> 00:14:37.663
Sorry for making you watch our stuff.

00:14:39.498 --> 00:14:40.666
It was a woman.

00:14:40.958 --> 00:14:42.001
I'm telling you, it was a man.

00:14:42.585 --> 00:14:43.836
It was a woman!

00:14:43.836 --> 00:14:44.712
It was a man!

00:14:44.962 --> 00:14:48.299
I swear it was a woman! I saw
long hair on the stretcher.

00:14:48.758 --> 00:14:51.218
There's a ton of men with long hair.

00:14:51.844 --> 00:14:55.139
Besides, no woman would
wear sneakers that big.

00:14:55.348 --> 00:14:57.850
<i>Stretcher? Did something happen?</i>
Maybe she was a woman that likes big sneakers.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:59.143
No way, man.

00:14:59.894 --> 00:15:02.063
Fine then, let's ask Ms. Minazuki.

00:15:02.521 --> 00:15:03.731
Oh, good call.

00:15:05.524 --> 00:15:10.613
You see, somebody collapsed and was carried
through the deck on a stretcher.

00:15:11.822 --> 00:15:14.325
We were wondering if the person
was a woman or a man.

00:15:15.368 --> 00:15:19.246
I'm sure you saw everything since you were out
there talking on the phone the whole time.

00:15:20.998 --> 00:15:22.917
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:15:22.917 --> 00:15:24.668
<i>Something like that happened while I was gone?</i>

00:15:25.628 --> 00:15:27.588
<i>So that’s why he was out there...</i>

00:15:28.672 --> 00:15:30.216
So, which was it?

00:15:31.133 --> 00:15:32.134
It was a man, right?

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:34.804
No, a woman, right?

00:15:35.971 --> 00:15:39.433
<i>These kids have noticed something.</i>

00:15:40.226 --> 00:15:41.727
<i>That must be it, I have to be careful.</i>

00:15:42.603 --> 00:15:45.189
<i>Even though they're kids, they're DDS students.</i>

00:15:46.232 --> 00:15:47.066
<i>They’re testing me.</i>

00:15:48.526 --> 00:15:52.696
<i>The aisle is so narrow that they must
have seen it pretty well themselves.</i>

00:15:53.948 --> 00:15:57.785
<i>They both know very well whether it was
a man or woman and they're testing me.</i>

00:15:59.078 --> 00:15:59.829
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:16:00.246 --> 00:16:01.664
<i>The odds are fifty-fifty.</i>

00:16:02.665 --> 00:16:04.500
<i>If I screw up, they'll dig deeper.</i>

00:16:05.709 --> 00:16:08.129
<i>I’m almost through this whole affair,</i>

00:16:08.129 --> 00:16:10.923
<i>I'm not going to mess it up now!</i>

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:14.051
Actually, I wasn't around.

00:16:16.137 --> 00:16:20.975
During that fuss over the sick person, I wasn't
on the deck;I was in the bathroom.

00:16:21.934 --> 00:16:24.728
So I don't know whether it was
a man or a woman. Sorry.

00:16:25.521 --> 00:16:26.772
Aww...

00:16:28.899 --> 00:16:31.610
Looks like Kyuu‘s reasoning was right.

00:16:32.987 --> 00:16:35.489
Ms. Minazuki... I didn't think it could be true,

00:16:36.949 --> 00:16:41.370
but you actually murdered your
ex-boyfriend, Mr. Taga.

00:16:43.038 --> 00:16:47.460
You pretended to be on the phone, but, in
reality, you got off the train and murdered him.

00:16:48.377 --> 00:16:49.712
That's why you weren't on the deck.

00:16:50.629 --> 00:16:51.547
Am I wrong?

00:16:54.175 --> 00:16:55.217
What are you talking about?

00:16:55.718 --> 00:16:57.511
I didn't know Mr. Taga was murdered.

00:16:58.304 --> 00:17:04.977
We just got a call from DDS, saying that Mr. Taga
was stabbed by someone near Nishiumigaoka.

00:17:05.853 --> 00:17:08.230
You are one of the suspects in this case.

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:09.899
Hold on!

00:17:10.649 --> 00:17:12.943
I've been on this train the whole time.

00:17:13.486 --> 00:17:14.528
What are you talking about?

00:17:14.904 --> 00:17:19.408
I explained that I was in the bathroom
during that fuss over the sick-person.

00:17:21.452 --> 00:17:23.245
No one fell ill.

00:17:25.456 --> 00:17:30.669
I was walking around because I heard
that a celebrity was in the next car.

00:17:31.670 --> 00:17:34.757
But you told yourself that I was out there...

00:17:34.757 --> 00:17:38.135
...because of the fuss over the sick person and
didn't realize that we were luring you in.

00:17:38.928 --> 00:17:43.849
Besides, you couldn't have been talking on the
phone for an entire hour. It's totally impossible.

00:17:45.726 --> 00:17:50.731
Your phone still had a full charge
when you showed it to us.

00:17:52.233 --> 00:17:56.362
When you're on the phone for an hour, your
battery loses its charge, at least a bit.

00:17:57.363 --> 00:17:59.782
Additionally, you have an older phone.

00:18:01.534 --> 00:18:05.287
Would you mind showing us your call history?

00:18:07.665 --> 00:18:09.458
I was lying when I said I was on the phone.

00:18:11.835 --> 00:18:12.670
You're right.

00:18:14.004 --> 00:18:17.007
The reason I went out was because
you guys were kind of annoying,

00:18:17.758 --> 00:18:20.553
so I went out to the deck to finish my drawing.

00:18:21.178 --> 00:18:23.472
That's why I just went along with your story.

00:18:23.889 --> 00:18:25.808
It's really bothersome to be randomly suspected.

00:18:26.684 --> 00:18:29.770
Here's my ticket; it's from the first station.

00:18:30.437 --> 00:18:32.481
I couldn't have this if I had gotten
off in between, right?

00:18:34.692 --> 00:18:36.860
Hey, what's this about, Kyuu?

00:18:37.736 --> 00:18:40.406
Kinta, that's a really simple trick.

00:18:42.157 --> 00:18:46.203
She got two tickets at the station
and put them through the gate.

00:18:46.912 --> 00:18:49.790
One ticket to the last stop, and
one to Nishiumigaoka.

00:18:51.041 --> 00:18:55.921
Even if you put two tickets through the automatic
gate at once, no one would think twice about it.

00:19:00.509 --> 00:19:01.969
Evidence?

00:19:02.678 --> 00:19:03.637
Do you have any evidence?

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:08.851
Do you have any evidence that
I committed the murder?

00:19:12.062 --> 00:19:13.647
Oh, you've got nothing to say to that?

00:19:14.189 --> 00:19:15.357
So, you don't have any, huh?

00:19:16.275 --> 00:19:19.778
All you do is pile assumption on top of
assumption! Is that what you learn at DDS?!

00:19:20.154 --> 00:19:21.905
If you don't stop, I'm really going to get angry.

00:19:22.489 --> 00:19:23.866
I have a rock-solid alibi!

00:19:23.866 --> 00:19:24.783
There's evidence.

00:19:26.035 --> 00:19:31.332
Earlier, you changed a drawing in front
of us. Can you show it to us again?

00:19:35.377 --> 00:19:36.587
Ms. Minazuki.

00:19:38.589 --> 00:19:39.381
Excuse me.

00:19:43.218 --> 00:19:45.554
This drawing's weird, don't you think?

00:19:47.014 --> 00:19:47.806
What is?

00:19:48.682 --> 00:19:49.350
The shadows.

00:19:50.934 --> 00:19:53.854
This shadow is extending towards the sun.

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:56.565
You're right. What's this about?

00:19:59.109 --> 00:20:02.237
It means that this red circle,
disguised as the sun,

00:20:04.406 --> 00:20:07.159
was already there when she took
the drawing out of the envelope.

00:20:09.828 --> 00:20:14.124
Because of that, you were forced to add
the lines and disguise it as the sun.

00:20:15.167 --> 00:20:18.128
Then, this red circle is... It couldn't be...

00:20:22.132 --> 00:20:23.384
It's Mr. Taga's blood.

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:29.723
Ever since you stuffed that envelope away,

00:20:30.307 --> 00:20:31.600
something's been bothering me.

00:20:31.975 --> 00:20:33.227
I suspect that there's some on it as well.

00:20:48.033 --> 00:20:48.992
Guess I'm unlucky...

00:20:51.537 --> 00:20:53.330
I rehearsed it many times.

00:20:59.878 --> 00:21:00.879
Ms. Minazuki...

00:21:01.588 --> 00:21:03.424
Why did you do something like this?

00:21:07.886 --> 00:21:12.015
He tossed me aside and proposed
to the girl who was my apprentice.

00:21:13.058 --> 00:21:13.726
On top of that, he...

00:21:14.351 --> 00:21:17.229
I won't be in charge of you anymore, so...

00:21:18.439 --> 00:21:21.567
Well, it means that your time's over.

00:21:26.530 --> 00:21:27.948
God damn him!

00:21:28.866 --> 00:21:31.326
Damn him!!!

00:21:34.413 --> 00:21:42.421
I was driven to a point where I had to choose
between either killing him or killing myself.

00:21:49.678 --> 00:21:53.474
Well, I don't think it's something
you kids would understand...

00:21:55.726 --> 00:21:58.896
We'll be arriving at the last
stop, Kamikeihan, shortly.

00:21:59.438 --> 00:22:02.858
Please be sure to take all
your belongings with you.

00:22:03.108 --> 00:22:04.568
The last stop, huh?

00:22:05.569 --> 00:22:07.988
I guess this is the last stop of my life.

00:22:09.156 --> 00:22:14.328
Ms. Minazuki, I really loved your books.

00:22:16.038 --> 00:22:20.459
When I was a kid, I didn't have a dad
and my mom was always out working.

00:22:22.085 --> 00:22:24.421
When I came home from school,
I always read your books.

00:22:25.923 --> 00:22:29.092
My favorite was the series about the
little mouse, Chip, and his family.

00:22:30.219 --> 00:22:34.807
Chip had a mother and father. They
all seemed so nice and happy.

00:22:35.974 --> 00:22:37.017
I loved it.

00:22:40.062 --> 00:22:43.774
So please, don't say that it's the end.

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:47.152
I want you to draw more of your
heart-warming picture books.

00:22:59.665 --> 00:23:01.834
Thank you, Little Master Detective.

00:23:13.929 --> 00:23:15.597
Let's get going.

00:23:20.978 --> 00:23:22.187
An e-mail from DDS.

00:23:24.898 --> 00:23:25.816
Hey, Kyuu.

00:23:26.984 --> 00:23:29.069
They saved Mr. Taga.

00:23:30.279 --> 00:23:32.531
Really? That's great!

00:23:33.240 --> 00:23:35.492
Yeah, let's go and relax now!

00:23:36.910 --> 00:23:37.536
Yeah!

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:47.385
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.385 --> 00:23:49.721
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.721 --> 00:23:52.390
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:54.059
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.059 --> 00:23:56.061
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.061 --> 00:23:58.355
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.355 --> 00:24:00.899
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.899 --> 00:24:02.692
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.401 --> 00:24:06.947
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.947 --> 00:24:10.575
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.618 --> 00:24:13.662
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.662 --> 00:24:16.081
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.081 --> 00:24:18.208
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.208 --> 00:24:19.751
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.210 --> 00:24:22.420
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.420 --> 00:24:24.631
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.131 --> 00:24:26.841
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.841 --> 00:24:30.345
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.137 --> 00:24:33.306
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.306 --> 00:24:35.225
EVEN WHEN WERE LOST...

00:24:35.225 --> 00:24:37.602
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.644 --> 00:24:40.438
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:24:47.439 --> 00:24:49.149
DDS Unsolved Case File:

00:24:49.524 --> 00:24:51.276
Karuizawa - Murdered Idol in a Sealed Room.

00:24:51.902 --> 00:24:55.030
When we get to the scene of the crime,
even our client has been assaulted.

00:24:55.697 --> 00:24:59.076
Yukihira, from class A, starts an
investigation to counter my own.

00:24:59.868 --> 00:25:02.037
Q vs. A - The Reasoning Battle Begins!

00:25:02.537 --> 00:25:03.956
Who'll solve it first?

00:25:12.347 --> 00:25:13.556
There's only one answer!
